# DTF tier manifest: conda-channel-types  (artifact-keeper#4708 / #4709 / #4711)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-conda (a stdlib-python
# static conda channel on the slot's own 172.16.<slot>.0/24 subnet, every
# document stamped with the marker "dtfmockconda<slot>").
#
# THE BUGS
# #4708  `repodata.json` branched on repository type, its four siblings did
#        not: current_repodata.json, run_exports.json, repodata.json.sig and
#        patch_instructions.json were always built from the repository's OWN
#        artifact rows. A Remote or Virtual has none, so a client asking a
#        remote/virtual channel for current_repodata got a well-formed EMPTY
#        channel (`{"packages":{}}`), run_exports lost every upstream entry,
#        the remote's .sig was 404 (or, on a signed virtual, a signature over
#        the empty hosted build that never verifies against the repodata.json
#        actually served), and patch_instructions.json was a 200 stub that
#        asserted "no patches" on behalf of a channel nobody asked.
# #4709  conda's security-relevant writes left no audit trail: native publish
#        (the handler inserts its own artifact row, bypassing the audited
#        ArtifactService path), withdraw, attestation verdicts, and stored
#        environment ingest/delete wrote zero audit_log rows.
# #4711  no metric told an operator that a virtual's allowlist was dropping
#        upstream records, that uploads carried install scripts, or how
#        attestation verdicts were going.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   anon GET /conda/{remote}/noarch/{current_repodata.json,run_exports.json,
#            patch_instructions.json,repodata.json.sig}     upstream bytes?
#   anon GET /conda/{virtual}/noarch/{current_repodata.json,run_exports.json,
#            patch_instructions.json}                       derived / merged / 404?
#   anon GET /conda/{signed virtual}/{keys/repo.pub, noarch/repodata.json(.sig)}
#            -> openssl dgst -sha256 -verify on the served bytes
#   PUT    /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}                    publish (x4)
#   DELETE /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}                    withdraw
#   PUT    /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}/attestation        malformed + unsigned
#   POST/DELETE /api/v1/repositories/{hosted}/environments  conda-lock.yml
#   PUT    /api/v1/repositories/{virtual}/allowlist         admit dtfup-alpha only
#   GET    /api/v1/admin/metrics                            Prometheus text
# Audit rows are read from audit_log in the slot's Postgres (they are written
# fire-and-forget, so each is polled for, then counted: exactly one per act).
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (CONTROL) true on BOTH images: the hosted channel's repodata.json and
#             current_repodata.json list its uploads; remote and virtual
#             repodata.json carry the upstream records; a hosted .sig with no
#             key is 404; withdraw, refused attestations and environment
#             ingest/delete answer as before; the allowlisted virtual's
#             repodata.json omits the non-admitted record; /api/v1/admin/metrics
#             answers.
#   (FIX)     #4708 remote siblings carry the mock's markers and the remote .sig
#             is the upstream's bytes; the virtual's current_repodata holds the
#             newest upstream version of each name and its run_exports holds
#             the remote's entry; virtual and hosted patch_instructions are
#             404; the signed virtual's .sig verifies against the repodata.json
#             it serves. #4709 one row each: ARTIFACT_UPLOADED (with
#             details.package coordinates), CONDA_PACKAGE_WITHDRAWN,
#             ATTESTATION_REJECTED (x2), ENVIRONMENT_REGISTERED,
#             ENVIRONMENT_DELETED. #4711 ak_conda_allowlist_dropped_total
#             {repository=<virtual>,member=<remote>},
#             ak_conda_install_script_findings_total{kind="post-link"},
#             ak_conda_attestation_total{outcome="rejected"|"absent"}.
#             All RED on 1.11.1: empty hosted-shape documents, 200 stubs, a
#             .sig that does not verify, zero audit rows, absent metrics.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~40 authenticated calls
# back to back (repo/member/allowlist/signing setup, four uploads, metric
# scrapes); the base default (ON) would turn a setup call into a 429.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the remote's upstream is the mock on a
# private address (the profile also sets it, and scopes the SSRF allowlist to
# 172.16.0.0/12).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
